 "notes": "The Gabinière islet off the south coast of Port-Cros; coastlines and the Gabinière Est dive-site point from OpenStreetMap. Layout from the Port-Cros national park site sheet and Saint P'Hyères Plongée: the east face drops over rock falls to sand at 45 m with the groupers at 15-25 m and barracuda at 10-20 m, boats moor in the Calanque Sombre on the north side, and the west face is a plateau to about 20 m with slabs and posidonia towards the south. The Dolmen lies about 60 m from the point above the Calanque Sombre (drawn off the north-east point, position approximate); the drift entry at the Calanque aux Loups is not placed because its position was not found. Wall, mooring and feature positions are approximate.",
